// TEST: Physics -- The Dynamical q: Quantum Chaos Reshapes the Partition Lattice
// ============================================================================
// Ex 29's verdict on classical cascades was INHERITED_NOT_DYNAMICAL: all
// fifteen connected 4-cumulants were negative, but reweighting the input
// jets flipped every sign -- the dynamics TRANSPORTS the state's fourth
// cumulant, it cannot reshape the pairing lattice. Its header then claimed,
// untested: "dynamical crossing suppression is a genuinely quantum
// signature". This example tests that claim -- same estimator, same
// mirrored control -- on an exactly diagonalized quantum spin chain.
// Setup: mixed-field Ising chain, L = 6 (d = 64), open ends,
//   H = sum sz_i sz_{i+1} - 1.05 sum sx_i + sum h_i sz_i,
// irregular fields h = (0.55, 0.71, 0.44, 0.68, 0.50, 0.62) (chaotic; the
// irregularity kills reflection parity) vs the h = 0 twin (transverse-
// field Ising, free-fermion INTEGRABLE). H, A = sx on site 1, B = sz on
// site 6 are built IN-LANGUAGE from Int64 bit algebra; the eigenfactors
// (E, V) are EMBEDDED but CERTIFIED in-file (ex 41's move: residuals
// |HV - VE|^2 and |VV^T - I|^2 pinned at ~1e-18 -- the external solve's
// provenance is proof-irrelevant). Time evolution needs no matrix
// exponential: in the eigenbasis A(t) = X + iY with X_ij = A~_ij cos((E_i
// - E_j) t), Y_ij = A~_ij sin(...), and every trace below is real by
// symmetry (X, B~ symmetric, Y antisymmetric). The estimator is ex 29's
// crossing channel verbatim on the time-ordered quadruple (A(t), B, A(t),
// B): kappa4 = p - 2 cab^2 - cAA cBB, qhat = 1 + kappa4/(cAA cBB) -- the
// crossing pairing (13)(24) IS the out-of-time-order contraction, so qhat
// is the normalized OTOC. State = infinite temperature tr(.)/64, the
// quantum analogue of ex 29's uniform grid.
// FINDINGS (pinned):
//   * DYNAMICAL CROSSING SUPPRESSION EXISTS. qhat(0) = 1 exactly (A and B
//     commute at t = 0); under chaotic evolution it collapses to the
//     scrambling floor by t ~ 5 and STAYS: six incommensurate late times
//     (the comb, t in [20, 38.6]) have mean 0.0891, variance 1.5e-4.
//   * THE LIGHT CONE GATES IT. qhat(0.5) = 1 to twelve digits: the
//     suppression cannot switch on before the Lieb-Robinson front crosses
//     the five bonds from A to B (ex 26's causal cone, quantum side).
//   * THE MIRRORED CONTROL FAILS TO FLIP IT -- the point of the file.
//     Deform the state's shape exactly as ex 29 deformed the jets:
//     thermal weights e^{-0.3 E} and a spectrally leptokurtic reweight
//     w ~ 1 + 3((E - mean)/sd)^2, both computed in-language from the
//     certified spectrum. The floor moves (0.089 -> 0.080 / 0.172) but
//     every kappa4 stays NEGATIVE -- 12/12 sign checks across two states
//     x six comb times. In ex 29 the same move flipped 15/15. The
//     suppression belongs to the DYNAMICS: DYNAMICAL_NOT_INHERITED.
//   * INTEGRABILITY IS THE CONTROL'S CONTROL. The free-fermion twin at
//     the same six late times: mean 0.470, variance 0.146 -- 950x the
//     chaotic comb variance, swinging -0.17..+0.96. Unitarity alone does
//     not scramble the crossing channel; chaos does (ex 17's persistence
//     dichotomy, fourth-order edition).
//   * THE SPECTRUM AGREES, IN-LANGUAGE: bulk consecutive-gap ratio
//     r = 0.4731 (toward GOE 0.536) vs 0.2919 (below Poisson 0.386:
//     exact free-fermion degeneracies) -- chaos certified from the same
//     embedded eigenvalues the estimator runs on.
// With ex 29 the dichotomy is closed on both sides: classical mixing
// transports kurtosis and cannot suppress crossings; quantum chaos
// suppresses crossings and the state cannot restore them. Honest scope:
// freeness-from-ETH / OTOC decay is known physics; new here is the arc's
// own estimator + mirrored control + integrable twin, exact and pinned in
// one self-certifying file. Every number was verified against an
// independent complex-matmul route (agreement ~1e-14) before pinning.
// ============================================================================

// ---- certified eigenfactors (emitted by the untrusted oracle; certified below) ----
// CSV-backed since 2026-07-19: the eigenfactors live in data/42_*.csv
// (bit-identical extraction of the former inline literals). Run from THIS
// directory so the relative paths resolve: `cd examples/physics && blade
// run 42_dynamical_q.blade` — see providers/CsvProviderSpec.md. The 1-D
// payloads are stored as one CSV row; `(0)` peels the vector off the
// 1 x 64 load.
import csv as csvd
let EC_h = csvd.load("data/42_EC.csv")
let EC_m = EC_h.vars.data |> csvd.read
let EC: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>> = EC_m(0)
let VC_h = csvd.load("data/42_VC.csv")
let VC: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>> = VC_h.vars.data |> csvd.read
let EI_h = csvd.load("data/42_EI.csv")
let EI_m = EI_h.vars.data |> csvd.read
let EI: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>> = EI_m(0)
let VI_h = csvd.load("data/42_VI.csv")
let VI: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>> = VI_h.vars.data |> csvd.read
// ---- Int64 bit algebra (all quantities non-negative: the signed-promotion
//      hazard never arises; spins/indicators exit through if-else) ----
function eqInd(a: Int64, b: Int64) -> Float64 = if a == b then 1.0 else 0.0
function spn(i: Int64, p: Int64) -> Float64 = if (i / p) % 2 == 0 then 1.0 else -1.0
function xorbit(i: Int64, p: Int64) -> Int64 = i + p - 2 * p * ((i / p) % 2)
// the five nearest-neighbour sz sz bonds of basis state i, and the six
// single-spin flips connecting i to j (the sx sum)
function bonds(i: Int64) -> Float64 = spn(i, 1) * spn(i, 2) + spn(i, 2) * spn(i, 4) + spn(i, 4) * spn(i, 8) + spn(i, 8) * spn(i, 16) + spn(i, 16) * spn(i, 32)
function flips(i: Int64, j: Int64) -> Float64 = eqInd(j, xorbit(i, 1)) + eqInd(j, xorbit(i, 2)) + eqInd(j, xorbit(i, 4)) + eqInd(j, xorbit(i, 8)) + eqInd(j, xorbit(i, 16)) + eqInd(j, xorbit(i, 32))

// ---- H, A, B in-language ----
let HC = method_for(range<Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) <@> lambda(i: Int64, j: Int64) -> eqInd(i, j) * (bonds(i) + 0.55 * spn(i, 1) + 0.71 * spn(i, 2) + 0.44 * spn(i, 4) + 0.68 * spn(i, 8) + 0.50 * spn(i, 16) + 0.62 * spn(i, 32)) - 1.05 * flips(i, j) |> compute
let HI = method_for(range<Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) <@> lambda(i: Int64, j: Int64) -> eqInd(i, j) * bonds(i) - 1.05 * flips(i, j) |> compute
let AX = method_for(range<Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) <@> lambda(i: Int64, j: Int64) -> eqInd(j, xorbit(i, 1)) |> compute
let BZ = method_for(range<Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) <@> lambda(i: Int64, j: Int64) -> eqInd(i, j) * spn(i, 32) |> compute

// ---- the per-model machinery, written once ----
// M N^T as the row-fiber product (rows of M against rows of N)
function mnt(m: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>, n: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) -> Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>> =
    method_for(m, n) <@> lambda(x: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>>, y: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>>) -> prodsum(x, y) |> compute
function transposed(m: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) -> Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>> =
    method_for(range<Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) <@> lambda(i: Int64, j: Int64) -> m(j, i) |> compute
// the Frobenius pairing sum_ij M_ij N_ij
function frob(m: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>, n: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) -> Float64 =
    reduce(method_for(zip(m, n)) <@> lambda(x: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>>, y: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>>) -> prodsum(x, y), (+))
// certification of an embedded eigenfactor (V, E) of h: |HV - VE|^2 and
// |V V^T - I|^2 (the eigenvectors are V's columns)
function eig_residual(h: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>, v: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>, e: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>>) -> Float64 = {
    let hv = mnt(h, transposed(v))
    let rs = method_for(range<Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) <@> lambda(i: Int64, j: Int64) -> hv(i, j) - v(i, j) * e(j) |> compute
    frob(rs, rs)
}
function orth_residual(v: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) -> Float64 = {
    let go = mnt(v, v)
    let dev = method_for(range<Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) <@> lambda(i: Int64, j: Int64) -> go(i, j) - eqInd(i, j) |> compute
    frob(dev, dev)
}
// an operator in the eigenbasis: V^T O V
function in_eigenbasis(o: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>, vt: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) -> Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>> =
    mnt(mnt(vt, o), vt)
// the bulk consecutive-gap ratio <min(g_k, g_k+1) / max(g_k, g_k+1)> over
// levels 12..51 (degenerate gaps count 0)
function gap_ratio(e: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>>) -> Float64 = {
    let gp = method_for(range<Idx<39>>) <@> lambda(k: Int64) -> e(k + 13) - e(k + 12) |> compute
    let rq = method_for(range<Idx<38>>) <@> lambda(k: Int64) -> (if gp(k) < gp(k + 1) then (if gp(k + 1) < 1.0e-12 then 0.0 else gp(k) / gp(k + 1)) else (if gp(k) < 1.0e-12 then 0.0 else gp(k + 1) / gp(k))) |> compute
    reduce(rq, (+)) / 38.0
}
// out-of-order steps in an ascending spectrum (0 for a sorted one)
function descents(e: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>>) -> Float64 =
    reduce(method_for(range<Idx<63>>) <@> lambda(k: Int64) -> if e(k + 1) < e(k) then 1.0 else 0.0, (+))

// ---- the estimator: ex 29's crossing channel at time t, infinite
//      temperature. In the eigenbasis A(t) = X + iY with X_ij =
//      A~_ij cos((E_i - E_j) t) and Y_ij = A~_ij sin(...); X and B~ are
//      symmetric, Y antisymmetric, so every trace is real:
//      qhat = tr(XBXB - YBYB)/64 - 2 (tr(XB)/64)^2 (unit normalizers) ----
function qhat(at: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>, bt: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>, e: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>>, t: Float64) -> Float64 = {
    let x = method_for(range<Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) <@> lambda(i: Int64, j: Int64) -> at(i, j) * cos((e(i) - e(j)) * t) |> compute
    let y = method_for(range<Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) <@> lambda(i: Int64, j: Int64) -> at(i, j) * sin((e(i) - e(j)) * t) |> compute
    let px = mnt(x, bt)
    let py = mnt(y, bt)
    let pa = frob(px, transposed(px))
    let pb = frob(py, transposed(py))
    let cb = frob(x, bt)
    (pa - pb) / 64.0 - 2.0 * (cb / 64.0) * (cb / 64.0)
}

// ---- model C (chaotic) and model I (integrable): certification,
//      eigenbasis observables, gap statistics ----
let VTC = transposed(VC)
let certC = eig_residual(HC, VC, EC)
let orthC = orth_residual(VC)
let monoC = descents(EC)
let ATC = in_eigenbasis(AX, VTC)
let BTC = in_eigenbasis(BZ, VTC)
let rstatC = gap_ratio(EC)
let VTI = transposed(VI)
let certI = eig_residual(HI, VI, EI)
let orthI = orth_residual(VI)
let monoI = descents(EI)
let ATI = in_eigenbasis(AX, VTI)
let BTI = in_eigenbasis(BZ, VTI)
let rstatI = gap_ratio(EI)

// ---- t = 0: the estimator opens at exactly 1 (commuting A, B) ----
let q0C = qhat(ATC, BTC, EC, 0.0)
let q0I = qhat(ATI, BTI, EI, 0.0)

// ---- chaotic sweep: light cone, arrival, collapse ----
let qc05 = qhat(ATC, BTC, EC, 0.5)
let qc1 = qhat(ATC, BTC, EC, 1.0)
let qc2 = qhat(ATC, BTC, EC, 2.0)
let qc3 = qhat(ATC, BTC, EC, 3.0)
let qc5 = qhat(ATC, BTC, EC, 5.0)

// ---- the late-time comb: six incommensurate times, chaotic and integrable ----
let qk1 = qhat(ATC, BTC, EC, 20.0)
let qk2 = qhat(ATC, BTC, EC, 23.7)
let qk3 = qhat(ATC, BTC, EC, 27.9)
let qk4 = qhat(ATC, BTC, EC, 31.3)
let qk5 = qhat(ATC, BTC, EC, 35.1)
let qk6 = qhat(ATC, BTC, EC, 38.6)

// ---- integrable twin: same estimator, same times ----
let qi2 = qhat(ATI, BTI, EI, 2.0)
let qi3 = qhat(ATI, BTI, EI, 3.0)
let qi5 = qhat(ATI, BTI, EI, 5.0)
let qm1 = qhat(ATI, BTI, EI, 20.0)
let qm2 = qhat(ATI, BTI, EI, 23.7)
let qm3 = qhat(ATI, BTI, EI, 27.9)
let qm4 = qhat(ATI, BTI, EI, 31.3)
let qm5 = qhat(ATI, BTI, EI, 35.1)
let qm6 = qhat(ATI, BTI, EI, 38.6)

// ---- comb statistics: floor + equilibration vs ringing ----
let QK = [qk1, qk2, qk3, qk4, qk5, qk6]
let QM = [qm1, qm2, qm3, qm4, qm5, qm6]
let meanK = reduce(QK, (+)) / 6.0
let varK = reduce((QK - meanK) * (QK - meanK), (+)) / 6.0
let meanM = reduce(QM, (+)) / 6.0
let varM = reduce((QM - meanM) * (QM - meanM), (+)) / 6.0

// ---- THE MIRRORED CONTROL: deform the state's shape (ex 29's reweighting
//      move), weights computed in-language from the certified spectrum ----
let WT0 = exp(0.0 - 0.3 * EC)
let WTH = WT0 / reduce(WT0, (+))
let eMean = reduce(EC, (+)) / 64.0
let eVar = reduce((EC - eMean) * (EC - eMean), (+)) / 64.0
let WL0 = 1.0 + 3.0 * (EC - eMean) * (EC - eMean) / eVar
let WLP = WL0 / reduce(WL0, (+))

// the weighted (state w) mean of a diagonal operator, its centered form,
// and the crossing channel with every trace taken in the state w
function wmean(w: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>>, o: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) -> Float64 =
    reduce(method_for(range<Idx<64>>) <@> lambda(k: Int64) -> w(k) * o(k, k), (+))
function centered(o: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>, m: Float64) -> Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>> =
    method_for(range<Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) <@> lambda(i: Int64, j: Int64) -> o(i, j) - m * eqInd(i, j) |> compute
function row_weighted(w: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>>, o: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) -> Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>> =
    method_for(range<Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) <@> lambda(i: Int64, j: Int64) -> w(i) * o(i, j) |> compute
// kappa4 of the time-ordered quadruple (A(t), B, A(t), B) in state w, with
// A(t) centered by its w-mean am and B centered (bc, its w-variance cbb):
// (kappa4, qhat) as a pair
function kappa_w(w: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>>, am: Float64, bc: Array<Float64 like Idx<64>, Idx<64>>, cbb: Float64, t: Float64) -> (Float64, Float64) = {
    let xc = method_for(range<Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) <@> lambda(i: Int64, j: Int64) -> ATC(i, j) * cos((EC(i) - EC(j)) * t) - am * eqInd(i, j) |> compute
    let yc = method_for(range<Idx<64>, Idx<64>>) <@> lambda(i: Int64, j: Int64) -> ATC(i, j) * sin((EC(i) - EC(j)) * t) |> compute
    let pc = mnt(xc, bc)
    let p2 = mnt(yc, bc)
    let caa = frob(row_weighted(w, xc), xc) + frob(row_weighted(w, yc), yc)
    let p1 = frob(row_weighted(w, pc), mnt(bc, xc))
    let p2t = frob(row_weighted(w, p2), mnt(bc, yc))
    let cab = wmean(w, pc)
    let kap = (p1 - p2t) - 2.0 * cab * cab - caa * cbb
    (kap, 1.0 + kap / (caa * cbb))
}

let aMT = wmean(WTH, ATC)
let bMT = wmean(WTH, BTC)
let BCT = centered(BTC, bMT)
let cBBT = frob(row_weighted(WTH, BCT), BCT)
let aML = wmean(WLP, ATC)
let bML = wmean(WLP, BTC)
let BCL = centered(BTC, bML)
let cBBL = frob(row_weighted(WLP, BCL), BCL)

let (kapt2, qt2) = kappa_w(WTH, aMT, BCT, cBBT, 23.7)
let (kapt4, qt4) = kappa_w(WTH, aMT, BCT, cBBT, 31.3)
let (kapt6, qt6) = kappa_w(WTH, aMT, BCT, cBBT, 38.6)
let (kapl2, ql2) = kappa_w(WLP, aML, BCL, cBBL, 23.7)
let (kapl4, ql4) = kappa_w(WLP, aML, BCL, cBBL, 31.3)
let (kapl6, ql6) = kappa_w(WLP, aML, BCL, cBBL, 38.6)

let meanTH = (qt2 + qt4 + qt6) / 3.0
let meanLP = (ql2 + ql4 + ql6) / 3.0

// ---- verdicts ----
let certV = if certC < 1.0e-16 && orthC < 1.0e-16 && certI < 1.0e-16 && orthI < 1.0e-16 && monoC < 0.5 && monoI < 0.5 then "EIGENFACTORS_CERTIFIED" else "NO"
let rstatV = if rstatC > 0.44 && rstatI < 0.35 then "GOE_VS_DEGENERATE_POISSON" else "NO"
let openV = if abs(q0C - 1.0) < 1.0e-9 && abs(q0I - 1.0) < 1.0e-9 then "OPENS_AT_WICK" else "NO"
let coneV = if abs(qc05 - 1.0) < 1.0e-9 then "SUPPRESSION_WAITS_FOR_THE_FRONT" else "NO"
let floorV = if varK < 0.01 && meanK < 0.15 then "FLOOR_EQUILIBRATED" else "NO"
let ringV = if varM > 0.01 then "INTEGRABLE_STILL_RINGING" else "NO"
// kappa4 sign census across the deformed states (the ex-29 flip test):
// at infinite temperature kappa4 = qhat - 1 (unit normalizer)
let KAPW = [kapt2, kapt4, kapt6, kapl2, kapl4, kapl6]
let nnegK = reduce(method_for(QK) <@> lambda(q) -> if q < 1.0 then 1.0 else 0.0, (+))
let nnegW = reduce(method_for(KAPW) <@> lambda(k) -> if k < 0.0 then 1.0 else 0.0, (+))
let robustV = if nnegK > 5.5 && nnegW > 5.5 then "K4_SIGN_ROBUST" else "PARTIAL_FLIP"
let verdictV = if nnegW > 5.5 then (if varK < 0.01 then "DYNAMICAL_NOT_INHERITED" else "NO") else "INHERITED"

// qhat(0) = 1 exactly; the front gates the collapse; the chaotic comb sits
// at the floor while the integrable twin rings; deforming the state moves
// the floor but flips nothing -- the mirror of ex 29's 15/15 flip:
// EXPECT: certC = 1.00508527626015e-24
// EXPECT: orthC = 7.57155843863209e-26
// EXPECT: certI = 8.01106504866241e-25
// EXPECT: orthI = 7.31276609949454e-26
// EXPECT: monoC = 0
// EXPECT: monoI = 0
// EXPECT: certV = "EIGENFACTORS_CERTIFIED"
// EXPECT: rstatC = 0.473059087594811
// EXPECT: rstatI = 0.291910646207281
// EXPECT: rstatV = "GOE_VS_DEGENERATE_POISSON"
// EXPECT: q0C = 1.00000000000004
// EXPECT: q0I = 1.00000000000004
// EXPECT: openV = "OPENS_AT_WICK"
// EXPECT: qc05 = 0.999999999999838
// EXPECT: coneV = "SUPPRESSION_WAITS_FOR_THE_FRONT"
// EXPECT: qc1 = 0.999999880468754
// EXPECT: qc2 = 0.988167771198188
// EXPECT: qc3 = 0.342668131715471
// EXPECT: qc5 = 0.0859055011155528
// EXPECT: qk1 = 0.0889630083580772
// EXPECT: qk4 = 0.102423351107015
// EXPECT: qk6 = 0.0658756259406985
// EXPECT: meanK = 0.0891410386672946
// EXPECT: varK = 0.000153278160263707
// EXPECT: floorV = "FLOOR_EQUILIBRATED"
// EXPECT: qi2 = 0.983609240263347
// EXPECT: qi3 = -0.0226291755878523
// EXPECT: qi5 = 0.5008972105721
// EXPECT: qm1 = 0.763657400451329
// EXPECT: qm4 = -0.171874073686762
// EXPECT: qm5 = 0.955613286775437
// EXPECT: meanM = 0.470487615826275
// EXPECT: varM = 0.146141898839132
// EXPECT: ringV = "INTEGRABLE_STILL_RINGING"
// EXPECT: kapt2 = -0.862916580981822
// EXPECT: qt2 = 0.0319527152156875
// EXPECT: qt4 = 0.0928431146731596
// EXPECT: qt6 = 0.0706813308879111
// EXPECT: meanTH = 0.0651590535922528
// EXPECT: kapl2 = -0.870703140480561
// EXPECT: ql2 = 0.126684143167515
// EXPECT: ql4 = 0.178283672822385
// EXPECT: ql6 = 0.168031474835728
// EXPECT: meanLP = 0.15766643027521
// EXPECT: nnegK = 6
// EXPECT: nnegW = 6
// EXPECT: robustV = "K4_SIGN_ROBUST"
// EXPECT: verdictV = "DYNAMICAL_NOT_INHERITED"
